meta-rzg3l-lp-display
=====================

Display on in system suspend for the RZ/G3L SMARC EVK. The CA55 (Cortex-A55)
sleeps and the DDR is in self-refresh, while the CM33 (Cortex-M33) keeps a low
power picture on screen from on-chip SRAM, with the module power updated every
second. USER_SW3 wakes the system; the Linux GUI is back on screen before
Linux has resumed.

Tested with Renesas RZ Linux BSP Plus for RZ/G3L (RZG3L-BSP-1.0.0), the
Multi-OS package, MACHINE = "smarc-rzg3l", eSD boot.


I. Changes
==========

  CM33      Bare-metal firmware (lpdemo-cm33-fw), started by BL2, runs from
            SRAM only. Measures the module power (ISL28022 on RIIC0), hands
            the running display over from Linux and back by switching the
            VSPD display list, redraws the power reading, and on USER_SW3
            takes the DDR out of self-refresh and wakes the CA55 (MHU).
  TF-A      System suspend mode PLAT_SYSTEM_SUSPEND=disp instead of vbat:
            BL31 puts the DDR into self-refresh and sleeps in SRAM. BL2
            copies the DDR retention parameters to SRAM.
  U-Boot    The boot logo and the display start at 1920x1080.
  Kernel    rz-du hands the display over to the CM33 on suspend and takes it
            back on resume, without a mode set. vsp1 and MIPI DSI keep
            running. RIIC0 is left to the CM33 (its clock stays on, i2c0 and
            audio are disabled). The shared SRAM is exposed through UIO.
  Apps      lpdemo-gui (GTK3, 1920x1080): power, 10 min chart and the
            "Enter Low Power" button. lpdemo-ctl: status, low power entry,
            test cycles.
  Image     lpdemo-image: core-image-weston plus the above. The eSD WIC
            image contains bl2, fip and the CM33 firmware.


II. Build
=========

Start from the BSP build environment of Renesas RZ Linux BSP Plus
(https://renesas-rz.github.io/rz_linux_bsp_plus/, RZ/G3L), with the
Graphics package and the Multi-OS package (How To Build, Step 3). Then add
the layers:

  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rz-features/meta-rz-multi-os/meta-rzg3l
  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-still
  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-lp-display

Set in conf/local.conf:

  USE_OPENAMP = "0"

Build:

  $ MACHINE=smarc-rzg3l bitbake lpdemo-image


III. Notes
==========

  - Enables MACHINE_FEATURES RZ_CM33_FIRMWARE_LOAD of the Multi-OS package.
  - Cannot be combined with meta-rzg3l-fast-boot (USB disabled) or
    meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-sequence.
  - bl2, fip, the CM33 firmware and the rootfs must come from the same
    build: they share the control block layout in SRAM
    (include/lpdemo_shared.h and lpdemo_shm.py, kept in sync by hand).
  - BL2 reads the CM33 firmware from boot media offset 0x270000 (eMMC boot
    partition 1, sector 0x1380). wic/lpdemo-bootpart-esd.wks puts it there.
  - The SLEEP button no longer wakes the system: wake-up is USER_SW3 only
    (or the timer of lpdemo-ctl).
  - With meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-cm33-anim, its animation is linked into
    this firmware (hooks in src/ext.h). SRAM 0x59C00-0x59FFF is reserved
    for it.
  - src/lp_glyphs.h (digits of the power reading) is generated offline by
    tools/gen_lp_glyphs.py, not in the Yocto build. Regenerate it after a
    change of the RPF1 layout in lpdemo_lpimage.py.
  - If the system does not wake up: lpdemo-ctl suspend --debug prints the
    BL31 and CM33 progress on the serial console.
